        <name>Info</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::GlobalsAAResult::FunctionInfo::Info</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>All of the information is encoded into a single pointer, with a three bit integer in the low three bits. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The high bit provides a flag for when this function may read any global. The low two bits are the <ref refid="namespacellvm_1a9db8c44b250b90e3ab7e4d144e7c9c2e" kindref="member">ModRefInfo</ref>. And the pointer, when non-null, points to a map from <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_global_value" kindref="compound">GlobalValue</ref> to <ref refid="namespacellvm_1a9db8c44b250b90e3ab7e4d144e7c9c2e" kindref="member">ModRefInfo</ref> specific to that <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_global_value" kindref="compound">GlobalValue</ref>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
